From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - use the fallback for associated data above 512 bytes

The response buffer for the associated data holds MAX_ASSOC_SIZE
bytes, so the driver fails a request with more:

  aead_enqueue() Error: associated data too long. (3346 > 512 bytes)
  alg: aead: gcm-aes-iproc encryption failed on test vector "random:
  alen=675 plen=5465 authsize=16 klen=32 novrfy=0"; expected_error=0,
  actual_error=-22, ...

The other implementations accept any length. Send such a request to
the fallback, which all the AEADs have.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 8 ++------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2716,12 +2716,8 @@ static int aead_enqueue(struct aead_request *req, bool is_encrypt)
 
 	flow_log("%s() enc:%u\n", __func__, is_encrypt);
 
-	if (req->assoclen > MAX_ASSOC_SIZE) {
-		pr_err
-		    ("%s() Error: associated data too long. (%u > %u bytes)\n",
-		     __func__, req->assoclen, MAX_ASSOC_SIZE);
-		return -EINVAL;
-	}
+	if (req->assoclen > MAX_ASSOC_SIZE)
+		return aead_do_fallback(req, is_encrypt);
 
 	if (ctx->is_esp && crypto_ipsec_check_assoclen(req->assoclen))
 		return -EINVAL;
